RDPSProbe 0.1
=============

A test program for the RISC OS RDP server project. It measures what an
RDP server would have to work with on this machine, and writes a report.

Double-click !RDPSProbe. A task window opens, runs the tests (about ten
seconds) and shows the report. The report is also saved as "Report"
inside !RDPSProbe: please send it back.

What it does:

- reads the screen mode (size, colours, where the screen is in memory);
- copies the whole screen into memory again and again for two seconds,
  to see how fast the screen can be read;
- does the same from memory to memory, for comparison;
- compares the screen with a copy, as a server looking for changes would;
- times a scan for changed 64x64 squares between two copies in memory;
- moves the mouse pointer a little way (OS_Word 21) and back, to check a
  remote mouse could move it.

Please run it in the desktop mode you'd use (the size and colours make a
difference), and leave the mouse still while it runs.

From the command line:  RDPSProbe [-p] [-t centiseconds] [-o file]
  -p  also try moving the mouse
  -t  how long to time each test (default 200)
  -o  save the report in a file too

Parts of this program were written with the help of an AI assistant.

